# t04_led_env_attack.ledc -- LED env CARRIER SHAPES and attack.  ~57 s
# NOT therapeutic.  Feature family: LED pulse envelope.
#
# env values the LED parser accepts (config_parser.c:1490-1494, 0..3; anything
# else including 4 falls back to 0):
#     0 SQUARE  1 SINE  2 TRIANGLE  3 TRAPEZOID (uses duty + attack)
# Documented harmonic ratios at 10 Hz / duty 50 / bright 100 / RGB 255
# (ledc_format.md, re-measured in led_audio_bug_sweep section 8/8a):
#     0  h2/h3/h4 = 0.004 / 0.345 / 0.003
#     1  0.084 / 0.020 / 0.052   (the raised-sine LUT; the old 4x(1-x) parabola
#                                  gave h3 = 0.145, 36x worse)
#     2  0.043 / 0.106 / 0.034
#     3  attack 3 ms -> h2 0.042 h3 0.316 ; 10 ms -> 0.221 / 0.221 ;
#        20 ms -> 0.360 / 0.061   (h2 rises and h3 falls monotonically with
#        attack -- that monotonic trend IS the test, not any single ratio)
#
# TWO TRAPS, both from led_audio_bug_sweep:
#  * PRINT h1 IN dBFS BESIDE EVERY RATIO.  A degraded signal path inflates EVEN
#    harmonics specifically; a 7 dB drop in the fundamental produced h2/h1 =
#    0.547 from a waveform that actually measures 0.044.  Passing signalcheck.py
#    is necessary but NOT sufficient.
#  * h5 of a 10 Hz flicker lands on 50 Hz mains.  Check that h5 MOVES when the
#    rate changes before believing it.
#
# Drive is 255 everywhere (RGB 255, bright 100) so the shape is not distorted by
# the low-drive roll-off -- a compressed dim end changes the harmonic ladder.
#
# NOTE ON `duty` UNDER env 1 AND env 2: it is IGNORED.  led_carrier_level_iram
# reads duty_q16 only in its TRAPEZOID branch; the sine branch is a pure raised
# sine from the LUT and the triangle branch is a fixed symmetric
# (ph<0.5)?2ph:2-2ph.  So the `50` in the duty column of B1 lane B and B2 lane A
# is inert, and a sine or triangle carrier always has a 50 % on-fraction.
# ledc_format.md annotates only env 3 as "uses duty+attack", which reads as if
# the others might honour it.  B1/B2 assert that they do not.
#
# lane A = mask 3 (capture ch4), lane B = mask 12 (capture ch3), distinct rates.
#
#
#
# CAPTURE-INTEGRITY CARRIER (audio ch15, 1900 Hz sine, hard LEFT, vol 40, from
# t=700 ms to the end of the file).  This is measurement scaffolding, not
# content.  A recorder can lose a block of frames mid-capture and still write a
# file of exactly the right length -- the missing TIME is simply absent -- and
# the frame-count check is blind to it.  Five such steps were found in one 665 s
# capture (~1 per 2.2 min), and one of them was written up as a firmware defect
# because BOTH optical sensors agreed on it: the whole recording had stepped.
#   python3 tools/avmeasure/captureintegrity.py rec.wav --carrier 1900 --audio-ch 1
# The tool needs a CONTINUOUS SINE: a session cycling square/saw/noise carriers
# gives ~369 us of phase noise against ~1 us for a sine, which inflates its
# self-calibrating threshold into a rubber stamp.  Hard LEFT so the RIGHT capture
# channel stays free of it for envelope and avsync work.  The marker window
# (0..600 ms) is not covered by this carrier; check it separately with
# --carrier 3000.
# CAPTURE-CHANNEL MAP used throughout sessions/test (see README.md):
#   capture ch1,ch2 = device headphone jack L,R   capture ch3 = photocell on
#   lane B's eye (LED3+LED4, mask 12)             capture ch4 = photocell on
#   lane A's eye (LED1+LED2, mask 3).
# --------------------------------------------------------------- sync marker
0     40 50 100 255 255 255 15
A 0   3000 0 70 0 1
600   -1 50 0 0 0 0 15
A 600 0 0 0 0 1

# ---- capture-integrity carrier: continuous 1900 Hz sine, ch15, hard LEFT
A 700 1900 -100 40 0 15 0 0

# ---- ISR TICK PRIMER.  The flicker gptimer is DELETED whenever no channel is
#      left running and the next activation re-derives its tick from the 1000 Hz
#      FLOOR, so the marker's `freq 0` stop at 600 ms RESETS it -- the 40 Hz
#      marker does NOT pin the tick.  Worse, an update on an already-running
#      channel never calls s_ensure_timer_and_task, so whatever the FIRST
#      post-marker block sets is what every later block gets.
#      This row keeps ONE channel alive at 40 Hz for the whole file, pinning the
#      tick at clamp(40*250,1000,10000) = 10000 Hz = a 100 us grid everywhere
#      below.  mask 16 = LED5, which neither sensor can see (-78 / -74 dBFS, the
#      noise floor), and brightness is 0 regardless, so it cannot contaminate a
#      measurement on any unit.  It raises LEDC_MASK_HIGH_BITS (info) by design.
1000 40 50 0 0 0 0 16 0 0

# ---- B1  1..11 s : env 0 SQUARE vs env 1 SINE
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0      # lane A: square, 10 Hz
1000  7 50 100 255 255 255 12 1 0      # lane B: sine,    7 Hz

# ---- B2  11..21 s : env 2 TRIANGLE vs env 3 TRAPEZOID at default attack
11000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  2 0     # lane A: triangle
11000  7 50 100 255 255 255 12 3 0 3   # lane B: trapezoid, attack 3 ms

# ---- B3  21..31 s : ATTACK SWEEP, 10 and 20 ms.  At 10 Hz / duty 50 the
#      duty/2 clamp sits at 25 ms, so both values are un-clamped and the
#      documented monotonic h2-up / h3-down trend applies.
21000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  3 0 10  # lane A: trapezoid, attack 10 ms
21000  7 50 100 255 255 255 12 3 0 20  # lane B: trapezoid, attack 20 ms

# ---- B4  31..43 s : LARGE ATTACK.  40 and 60 ms only mean anything if duty/2
#      exceeds them, so the rates drop: 4 Hz duty 50 -> clamp 62.5 ms, 3 Hz duty
#      50 -> clamp 83 ms.  Both edges are therefore real, not clamped.
31000 4 50 100 255 255 255 3  3 0 40   # lane A: 4 Hz, attack 40 ms (48 cycles)
31000 3 50 100 255 255 255 12 3 0 60   # lane B: 3 Hz, attack 60 ms (36 cycles)

# ---- B5  43..55 s : TWO CLAMPS.
#      lane A: attack 80 ms.  led_matrix_set_attack_masked caps at 60 ms
#      (led_matrix_example.c:1497), so this must measure IDENTICALLY to lane A
#      of B4 scaled -- i.e. to a 60 ms edge, NOT an 80 ms one.
#      lane B: env 4 on an LED line.  The parser maps anything outside 0..3 to
#      0, so this must measure as SQUARE -- same ladder as B1 lane A.
43000 4 50 100 255 255 255 3  3 0 80   # lane A: attack 80 -> capped to 60
43000 3 50 100 255 255 255 12 4 0      # lane B: env 4 -> square

# ---- end
55000 -1 50 0 0 0 0 15
55000 -1 50 0 0 0 0 16                     # stop the tick primer too
A 55000 1900 -100 0 0 15 0 0            # stop the integrity carrier
